From: =?UTF-8?q?L=C3=A9onard?= <leonard@synthe.se>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:49:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] net: bcmgenet: Do not touch the EEE registers on GENET v1
 and v2

Since commit a9f31047baca ("net: bcmgenet: Fix EEE implementation"),
bcmgenet_eee_enable_set() runs on every link change, whatever the GENET
version: it reads and writes UMAC_EEE_CTRL, TBUF_ENERGY_CTRL and
RBUF_ENERGY_CTRL. On a GENET v2 (BCM7231), the first link-up then raises
a fatal GISB bus error.

The ethtool EEE operations already return -EOPNOTSUPP on GENET v1.
Return early from bcmgenet_eee_enable_set() on v1 and v2, so that link
changes no longer reach these registers there.

Fixes: a9f31047baca ("net: bcmgenet: Fix EEE implementation")
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/genet/bcmgenet.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/genet/bcmgenet.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/genet/bcmgenet.c
index f4cfbff..8e2047b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/genet/bcmgenet.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/genet/bcmgenet.c
@@ -1364,6 +1364,12 @@ void bcmgenet_eee_enable_set(struct net_device *dev, bool enable)
 	u32 off = priv->hw_params->tbuf_offset + TBUF_ENERGY_CTRL;
 	u32 reg;
 
+	/* No EEE control on GENET v1 and v2: touching these registers raises
+	 * a bus error.
+	 */
+	if (GENET_IS_V1(priv) || GENET_IS_V2(priv))
+		return;
+
 	if (enable && !priv->clk_eee_enabled) {
 		clk_prepare_enable(priv->clk_eee);
 		priv->clk_eee_enabled = true;
